GitHub Branch Management – Viva Questions
Basic questions
1. What is GitHub?

GitHub is an online platform used to store, manage and share source code.

2. What is Git?

Git is a version control system. Code lo changes ni track cheyadaniki use chestham.

3. What is a repository?

Repository is a place where project files and code are stored.

4. What is a branch?

Branch is a separate working area. Main code disturb cheyakunda new features develop cheyochu.

5. What is the main branch?

main is the primary branch. Usually production-ready code ikkada maintain chestham.

6. What is a develop branch?

Develop branch is used to combine and test new features before adding them to main.

7. Why do we create branches?

Main code affect kakunda separate ga development cheyadaniki branches create chestham.

Branch management questions
8. How do you create a new branch in GitHub?

Branch dropdown click chesi, new branch name enter chesi Create branch click chestham.

9. What is a feature branch?

Feature branch is used to develop a particular functionality.

Example: feature/login.

10. What is a Pull Request?

Pull Request (PR) is a request to merge changes from one branch into another branch.

11. What is merging?

Merging means combining changes from one branch into another branch.

12. What is a merge conflict?

Two branches lo same code lines different ga modify ayinappudu merge conflict occur avvachu.

13. Can we delete a branch after merging?

Yes. Merge ayyaka unnecessary feature branches delete cheyochu.

14. What is the difference between main and develop?

Main – Production-ready code.

Develop – New features integration and testing.

15. What is a commit?

Commit is a saved snapshot of changes in the repository.

